# Voxel Flyover: a corgi on a jet surfboard, a pelican on a bicycle pedalling under it for the
# jets, flies over a planet that can be left, a sphere of 600,000 units
# drawn by Godot's Forward+ renderer on gpu@0. Its world is a function its shaders compute at
# the points of the sphere: a pass draws the ground into textures as the flight goes, and the
# vertex stages raise grids of land to it, out to the horizon and round the planet. Its project
# (demos/godot/voxel-flyover) is imported and exported here by Godot's editor, and voxel-flyover
# plays the pack with godot, which installs with it. The project installs too. The flyer, the
# board with the corgi and the pelican on its bicycle, is made by Blender from the project's
# flyer.py into flyer.glb, which the game reads when it starts: Blender run on the script again
# makes it anew.
FROM /Dollyfile-system 8d54b8fd95bd265381fcacf4d97044d3ad3deb0e969deeed8e4b5e791e71dcb5
INSTALL /demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot a07eb1a7b241b23dd68aa49582ca0338d8949ff94273d58b8f2010b2c764305e
USE /demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot-editor 41a3f6f8e56c4de02b5a9498ffd4be8bf8ac37780d7215b9e1a15e72af4c7a5e
USE /demos/blender/Dollyfile-blender c7162bd0097e17bd6ceaa9644694d7aa5bfeca853f12834d00ce01a31bfd5dda

REQUIRES TOOL blender
REQUIRES TOOL cp
REQUIRES TOOL godot-editor
